<title>UK: Black Sea Novorossiisk oil port shut due to swell.</title>
<headline>Black Sea Novorossiisk oil port shut due to swell.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Black Sea port of Novorossiisk was closed on Monday due to a heavy swell, shipping inspector Petrak said.</p>
<p>The port was closed at 2320 local time on Sunday due to swells ranging 1.3 to two metres, Petrak said.</p>
<p>On Monday morning one crude tanker was alongside waiting to load and another three were at anchor waiting to berth.</p>
<p>All other Black Sea and Baltic ports exporting Russia oil were operating normally, Petrak said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7714</p>
